comments:
I was able to debug this with `systemd-dissect` (debugging PID1 with gdb is damn hard, one mistake and it's reboot time which isn't great since the system has trouble booting with the bug). The error happens in call to [blkid_safeprobe()](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/a27c229c15830895d712ab338a22ef0ec4564ce2/src/shared/dissect-image.c#L745).

I think the problem is that libblkid is using buffers which aren't aligned enough in [libblkid/src/probe.c#L562](https://github.com/karelzak/util-linux/blob/0a08200bd5664d1849e477f7f776ab4d13bb8422/libblkid/src/probe.c#L562):
```c
	/* allocate info and space for data by one malloc call */
	bf = calloc(1, sizeof(struct blkid_bufinfo) + len);
	if (!bf) {
		errno = ENOMEM;
		return NULL;
	}

->	bf->data = ((unsigned char *) bf) + sizeof(struct blkid_bufinfo);
	bf->len = len;
	bf->off = real_off;
	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&bf->bufs);

	DBG(LOWPROBE, ul_debug("\tread: off=%"PRIu64" len=%"PRIu64"",
	                       real_off, len));

->	ret = read(pr->fd, bf->data, len);
```

Perhaps the allocation should use `posix_memalign()`, alignment should be increased manually (since there's already some pointer arithmetic going on) or perhaps even the caller could donate a suitably aligned buffer. @karelzak WDYT?

